<title>SPAIN: Acciona group wins 70 bln pta contract.</title>
<headline>Acciona group wins 70 bln pta contract.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Acciona STU Servicios Tecnicos Urbano said on Thursday a consortium in which it has a 40 percent stake has won a 20-year contract for the management of Valladolid's city water services, worth 70 billion pesetas ($479.6 million), with average annual billings of 3.5 billion pesetas, Acciona said.</p>
<p>In addition to Acciona, consortium participants are: Interagua, a venture of Aguas de Barcelona, Endesa and Argentaria with 40 percent; and Aquagest, a company of Aguas de Barcelona with the remaining 20 percent.</p>
<p>The contract takes effect on July 1 for 20 years.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167 ($ = 145.9 Spanish Pesetas)</p>
